# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files — never commit real environment values (.env.example IS committed)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# test output
coverage/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# Figma audit working directory — device screenshots and Figma renders (~75 MB of PNGs).
# Deliberately NOT committed: every measurement, node value, classification and verdict derived
# from these images is written into docs/FIGMA_PIXEL_PERFECT_AUDIT.md, Figma remains the live
# source of truth for the renders, and nothing in the build or at runtime reads this directory
# (it is already excluded from Prettier for the same reason). Kept on disk locally.
.figma-audit/
